  "starterCode": "# BPE Encode/Decode — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(text, merges):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **BPE Encode/Decode** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef solution(text, merges):\n    tokens=list(text)\n    for left,right,merged in merges:\n        out=[]; i=0\n        while i<len(tokens):\n            if i+1<len(tokens) and tokens[i]==left and tokens[i+1]==right:\n                out.append(merged); i+=2\n            else: out.append(tokens[i]); i+=1\n        tokens=out\n    return {\"tokens\":tokens,\"decoded\":\"\".join(tokens)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
